{
  "id": "title-panorama",
  "name": "A Famosa — title panorama",
  "notes": [
    "THE TITLE SCREEN, AND THE LOADING SCREEN DERIVED FROM IT.",
    "",
    "This is a SCREEN, not a world: no walk mask, no spawns, no transitions, no",
    "collision. tools/forge/title-screen.cjs composes it, runs it through the",
    "dusk LUT (and the night LUT for the calmer loading variant), bakes the lamp",
    "pass, and installs the x3 upscales over assets/scenes/opening-screen.png and",
    "assets/scenes/scene-loading-ribeira.png.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED AT 320x180, the original spec resolution, shipped at an exact x3 to",
    "960x540. The world plates run 640x360 native because the camera scrolls over",
    "them; a title screen is one static frame filling the viewport exactly, so the",
    "chunkier grid is the right one — and 640x360 would need a 1.5x upscale, which",
    "is not an integer and would smear the pixel grid the whole game is built on.",
    "",
    "NO TEXT IS BAKED IN. The old plate had 'A FAMOSA' and 'MELAKA 1580' painted",
    "into it, which is why .ui-screen-scrim had to be fully OPAQUE in a band top",
    "and bottom — otherwise the baked type ghosted through behind the real React",
    "chrome. With the type gone the scrim goes back to an even veil and the whole",
    "panorama reads.",
    "",
    "THE COMPOSITION, left to right: the church hill with its bell tower on the",
    "crest; the town's roofs going down to the water; A Famosa's keep on the right",
    "shoulder; the roadstead with a Fujian junk, a Gujarati dhow and the lighters",
    "working between them; the quay in the near foreground with its lamps lit."
  ],
